The plate is a square dinner plate, roughly 26 cm across, holding a small pile of roasted green beans. The pile covers about 12 × 8 cm and is a couple of layers thick, so I estimate about 60-70 g of beans.

Green beans are roughly 35 kcal per 100 g. These look roasted with some oil, so I'll use about 80 kcal per 100 g. That gives around 65 g × 0.8 ≈ 52 kcal, and I'll round up to about 55 kcal to allow for the oil.

